    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9312" root="حنط" body-key="H">
    
      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حنّطهُ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَحْنِيطٌ</span> (S, TA;) in the K,
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَنَطَهُ</span></b> , aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَنُطَ</span></b> ; which is a mistake; (TA;) <i>He
prepared him</i> (a dead person [i. e. <i>for burial</i>])
[and also <i>it</i> (grave-clothing)] <i>with</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَنُوط</span> [q. v.];
(S, K;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">احنطهُ</span></b> . (K.) And [hence,]
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُحْنِطَ</span></b>  [lit. <i>He was prepared for burial with</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حنوط</span>, is used to signify] <i>he died.</i> (K.)

